    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** stands as the definitive anchor for Ghost Ride the WHIP with an elite score of 85.84. Facing Ure\u00f1a, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a prime number three spot in the order and a favorable park factor, but his primary value remains the high-end xwOBA that maximizes his stolen base potential in this matchup. Similarly, **James Wood** is a must-start at 76.28. Leading off against the high-xERA Spence, **James Wood** profiles as our best source of counting stats today; his elite 0.403 xwOBA, paired with the SP Skill boost, positions him to capitalize on the weak opposing starter. While **Gabriel Moreno** and **Tyler Soderstrom** offer solid mid-range utility, the secondary tier of our lineup\u2014specifically **Zach McKinstry**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Kyle Karros**\u2014remains marginal, hovering near the 40-50 efficiency floor due to bottom-third batting order placement and tougher SP matchups like Imanaga.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card involved balancing **Dalton Rushing** against the potential of deeper roster depth. Despite his 55.40 score, **Dalton Rushing** was kept in the lineup primarily due to positional scarcity, though the optimization algorithm flagged a significant 8% penalty due to his #8 batting position and a 40% SB hold expectation against the opposing pitcher. We are effectively punting the bottom of the order to preserve game caps, as no healthy bench assets like **Brice Turang** or **Austin Riley** are available to swap in due to scheduling conflicts or team off-days. Note that **Mickey Moniak** and **Trevor Story** remain on the IL, limiting our ability to pivot away from the sub-50 scores of **Zach McKinstry** and **Alex Freeland**. While **Seiya Suzuki** provides a reliable floor of 63.62 against Lorenzen, we will be monitoring for any late-inning weather alerts, though currently, the primary risk remains the stagnant lineup construction caused by the mid-week schedule congestion for players like **Jose Caballero** and **Josh Naylor**.",
